about 2 000 tons of cocaine are produced  every year that's almost double the  amount that was made a decade ago and  Colombia is at the heart of this boom  satellite photos showed that about 200  000 hectares of land were used for Coca  last year that's five times more than  there were at the height of Pablo  Escobar's Medellin cartel the global  Fallout is showing up everywhere from  the warehouses of Antwerp to coup plots  in West Africa bringing violence  corruption and big profits Bloomberg  reporter Matthew Bristow traveled to  putomayo province in southern Colombia  and visited an eight hectare coca farm  that sells about 40 kilograms of the  drug a year one kilo sells between  thirty thousand dollars in the U.S to  160 thousand dollars in Australia the  farmers make about just over six hundred  dollars for every kilogram that they  produce which isn't very much given that  they also have to pay for all the  chemicals they have to pay for gasoline  so they're left with very little in the  way of profits Colombian cocaine  production began Rising 10 years ago  when the government started negotiations  with the largest Guerrilla group the  farc cocoa production roughly has  tripled since then during the peace  talks the government reduced the amount  of eradication of Coker it was doing the  piece of talks was supposed to lead to  drop in Cocoa production but when the  gorilla is demobilized the areas that  they occupied were filled by new illegal  arms groups and these groups often  threatened to kill people for  cooperating with government programs to  eradicate coca Bill Farms are still  being targeted the new president Gustavo  Petro proposed a different approach to  the war on drugs he says the War on  Drugs pursued by Bogota and Washington  for decades has brought violence to  Latin America while failing to stem  death and addiction in the United States  he wants to go after the mafia and big  shipments of cocaine rather than the  poorest coca farmers  [M